{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user wants me to implement a `solve(case)` function for task DATA-HDB-01. Let me analyze what's needed:\n\n1. Given nodes, core_distance dict, and distances list\n2. Compute mutual reachability: max(core_dist[u], core_dist[v], distance(u,v))\n3. Build MST using Kruskal's algorithm with deterministic tie-breaking\n4. Return mst_edges and total_weight\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    import math\n    \n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    core_distance = case[\"core_distance\"]\n    distances = case[\"distances\"]\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid nodes\")\n    if not isinstance(core_distance, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid core_distance\")\n    if not isinstance(distances, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid distances\")\n    \n    # Check all nodes have core distances\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node {node} missing from core_distance\")\n    \n    n = len(nodes)\n    \n    # Compute mutual reachability for each edge\n    mr_edges = []\n    for edge in distances:\n        u, v, d = edge[0], edge[1], edge[2]\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\n        # Canonicalize: sort endpoints\n        if u \u003e v:\n            u, v = v, u\n        mr_edges.append((mr, u, v))\n    \n    # Sort by mutual reachability, then by endpoint IDs\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\n    \n    # Kruskal's MST with union-find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    mst_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    \n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr])\n            total_weight += mr\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\n                break\n    \n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected, cannot form MST\")\n    \n    return {\n        \"mst_edges\": mst_edges,\n        \"total_weight\": total_weight\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the canonicalization step - when I swap u and v for ordering purposes, I need to make sure the output uses the canonical form. Let me re-read the instructions.\n\n\"Canonicalize undirected endpoints.\" - So I should canonicalize (sort) the endpoints.\n\nAlso for the sort: \"Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs\" - so sort by (mr, u, v) after canonicalization.\n\nLet me also check the output format - mst_edges should be arrays of [string, string, number]. The weight in each edge should be the mutual reachability weight.\n\nLet me also verify with the first test case manually:\n- nodes: p0, p1, p2, p3, p4\n- core_distance: p0=0.23243377, p1=0.50398147, p2=0.55673811, p3=0.66828478, p4=0.43968915\n- distances: various\n\nFor p0-p1: max(0.23243377, 0.50398147, 0.89672724) = 0.89672724\nFor p0-p2: max(0.23243377, 0.55673811, 0.73968893) = 0.73968893\nFor p0-p3: max(0.23243377, 0.66828478, 0.77270596) = 0.77270596\nFor p0-p4: max(0.23243377, 0.43968915, 0.87376631) = 0.87376631\nFor p1-p2: max(0.50398147, 0.55673811, 1.08418122) = 1.08418122\nFor p1-p3: max(0.50398147, 0.66828478, 0.82719237) = 0.82719237\nFor p1-p4: max(0.50398147, 0.43968915, 0.61293041) = 0.61293041\nFor p2-p3: max(0.55673811, 0.66828478, 1.00286271) = 1.00286271\nFor p2-p4: max(0.55673811, 0.43968915, 0.5322912) = 0.55673811\nFor p3-p4: max(0.66828478, 0.43968915, 0.51351834) = 0.66828478\n\nSorted by (mr, u, v):\n1. (0.55673811, p2, p4)\n2. (0.61293041, p1, p4)\n3. (0.66828478, p3, p4)\n4. (0.73968893, p0, p2)\n5. (0.77270596, p0, p3)\n...\n\nKruskal's:\n1. Add (p2, p4, 0.55673811) - union p2, p4. Components: {p0}, {p1}, {p2,p4}, {p3}\n2. Add (p1, p4, 0.61293041) - union p1, find(p4)=p2's root. Components: {p0}, {p1,p2,p4}, {p3}\n3. Add (p3, p4, 0.66828478) - union p3, find(p4). Components: {p0}, {p1,p2,p3,p4}\n4. Add (p0, p2, 0.73968893) - union p0 with find(p2). Components: {p0,p1,p2,p3,p4}\n\nMST edges: [(p2,p4,0.55673811), (p1,p4,0.61293041), (p3,p4,0.66828478), (p0,p2,0.73968893)]\nTotal weight = 0.55673811 + 0.61293041 + 0.66828478 + 0.73968893 = 2.57764223\n\nThis looks reasonable. Let me write the final implementation.\n\nOne thing to note: in the output, the edge nodes should be in canonical (sorted) order. The edge format is [string, string, number].\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me write it as a properly escaped JSON string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    core_distance = case[\\\"core_distance\\\"]\\n    distances = case[\\\"distances\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes must be a non-empty list\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(core_distance, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"core_distance must be a dict\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(distances, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"distances must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node {node!r} missing from core_distance\\\")\\n\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n\\n    # Compute mutual reachability for each edge and canonicalize endpoints\\n    mr_edges = []\\n    for edge in distances:\\n        u, v, d = edge[0], edge[1], edge[2]\\n        if u not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node {u!r} in distances not in core_distance\\\")\\n        if v not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node {v!r} in distances not in core_distance\\\")\\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        # Canonicalize: lexicographic order\\n        if u \u003e v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        mr_edges.append((mr, u, v))\\n\\n    # Sort by mutual reachability, then by endpoint IDs for determinism\\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\\n\\n    # Union-Find (path compression + union by rank)\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        root = x\\n        while parent[root] != root:\\n            root = parent[root]\\n        # Path compression\\n        while parent[x] != root:\\n            parent[x], x = root, parent[x]\\n        return root\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\\n        parent[ry] = rx\\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n\\n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr])\\n            total_weight += mr\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Input graph is disconnected; MST cannot be formed\\\")\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges,\\n        \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_014idHDc1nrx0u7i549jPPOt","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2393,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":60,"output_tokens":2565,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1797},"service_tier":"standard"}}